exonerate
------------------------------------------
Exonerate is a generic tool for sequence alignment, allowing rapid comparison
of biological sequences using many alignment models.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libglib2.0_0-2.90.1-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20261107-1
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libglib2.0-devel-2.90.1-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/nathanweeks/exonerate

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/nathanweeks/exonerate/archive/refs/tags/v2.4.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack exonerate-2.4.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./exonerate-2.4.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/exonerate-2.4.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/exonerate-2.4.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

